      en: "The Central Bank of São Tomé and Príncipe (BCSTP) is the heart of the country's financial system. It was established in 1976, one year after independence, to ensure monetary stability and guide economic policy. Its modern building in the financial district of São Tomé symbolizes the nation's economic sovereignty. The bank's main tasks include issuing and managing the national currency, the Dobra (STD), regulating the banking sector, and managing foreign exchange reserves. It plays a crucial role in implementing reforms and cooperating with international financial institutions like the IMF and the World Bank to promote the economic development of the small island nation."
