      en: "São Tomé International Airport (IATA: TMS) is the only international gateway to the archipelago. It is located north of the capital, right on the coast. The runway stretches along the Atlantic, offering spectacular views on arrival and departure. The airport was originally built by the Portuguese and has been modernized several times since independence. It handles flights to destinations in Africa (e.g., Lisbon via Accra, Luanda, Libreville) and Europe. The terminal is small but functional. The airport is crucial for tourism, the country's most important growth industry, as well as for cargo traffic that supplies the islands with vital goods. Its location makes it vulnerable to coastal erosion, requiring constant protective measures."
